}{\plain \fs24 \tab For at least a hundred years, the sprawling cross-cultural comparative studies of the 19}{\plain \fs24 \super th}{\plain \fs24  \softline
century linked with the Frazers, Tylors and Robertson Smiths of the day have come in for sharp \softline
criticism. In 1903 review of Edgar Crawley{\u8217\'92}s }{\plain \fs24 \ul Mystic Rose}{\plain \fs24  (itself dedicated to Frazer), Durkheim \softline
spared the method of Frazer no ridicule:(Stocking 1987, p. 173):\par
}\pard \fs24\li720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920 
{\plain \fs24 {\u8220\'93}One certainty finds interesting insights there. But, to a rare degree, the method lacks a \softline
critical and discriminating character.  In order to prove an assertion, the author does not \softline
hesitate to gather together, without distinguishing between them, facts borrowed from the \softline
most heterogeneous societies.  All the continents are scoured without order or \softline
discrimination.{\u8221\'94}(Lukes 1972, p. 451)\par
}\pard \fs24\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920
{\plain \fs24 \par
}\pard \fs24\fi720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920 
{\plain \fs24 \tab Yet, despite such criticism of them, the classic 19}{\plain \fs24 \super th}{\plain \fs24  century comparativists  represented a \softline
paradigm of ambitious, full-bore comparative study, and as such constituted a subspecies of what \softline
I shall call {\u8220\'93}strong{\u8221\'94} programs in comparative studies. The question that drives this present \softline
discussion is whether, once thus discredited, a {\u8220\'93}strong program{\u8221\'94} of comparative study of equal or \softline
similar ambition to that of the classic theorists can withstand critical epistemological assault? \softline
Perhaps the discrediting of the classic {\u8220\'93}strong program{\u8221\'94} has doomed }{\plain \fs24 \ul any}{\plain \fs24  }{\plain \fs24 \ul method}{\plain \fs24  of {\u8220\'93}strong{\u8221\'94} \softline
comparative study?  I do not think this is so, and will try to convince readers that a {\u8220\'93}strong \softline
program{\u8221\'94} in comparative studies is not only possible and desirable, but also practiced with \softline
success in some fields of the humanities.\par
}{\plain \fs24 Jonathan Z. Smith throws open the question of the status and nature of comparative study \softline
in a fruitful way by arguing that three fundamental questions need to be addressed about \softline
comparative studies if, in effect, the ambitions of the 19}{\plain \fs24 \super th}{\plain \fs24  century theorists were to be revived: \softline
{\u8220\'93}How{\u8221\'94} do we compare? {\u8220\'93}why?{\u8221\'94} and {\u8220\'93}so what?{\u8221\'94}  Smith here no doubt implicitly acknowledges \softline
Gopala Sarana{\u8217\'92}s identical list of demands, which in Sarana{\u8217\'92}s handy discussion of the \softline
methodology of anthropological comparison are answered in a variety of ways(Sarana 1975, ch. \softline
3).  I take these questions to be critical as well, but wish to press on beyond Smith, Sarana and \softline
others to celebrate a preferred method of {\u8220\'93}how{\u8221\'94} to do comparative studies, a justification for why \softline
to do them, and thus silence the charge of {\u8220\'93}so what?  Taking these queries in order, I shall argue \softline
that }{\plain \fs24 \ul hypothesis testing}{\plain \fs24  ultimately constitutes the main }{\plain \fs24 \ul purpose}{\plain \fs24  for doing comparative studies in \softline
the {\u8220\'93}strong{\u8221\'94} sense; {\u8220\'93}}{\plain \fs24 \ul how}{\plain \fs24 {\u8221\'94} things are to be compared and tested is well (even if not exclusively) \softline
exemplified by the program of comparative study systematically articulated by the Durkheimian \softline
{\u8220\'93}nucleus{\u8221\'94}, and interpreted thereafter by historians of the }{\plain \fs24 \ul Annales}{\plain \fs24  school like Marc Bloch and \softline
Lucien Febvre.  To answer {\u8220\'93}}{\plain \fs24 \ul so what}{\plain \fs24 ?{\u8221\'94} is to speak directly to the quality of the various \softline
intellectual strategies and values of intellectual workers in the human sciences bring to their uses \softline
of comparisons. In general, then little more can be specified here in advance of the unrolling of \softline
various projects employing comparison. It all depends on how comparisons are used. And, that 
depends in part on the virtuosity of those who do the comparing, and in part on the issue selected \softline
in comparisons.\par
}\pard \fs24\fi720\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920 
